# Infrastructure Layer

Outermost layer of the Onion. Persistence adapters, web routers (FastAPI),
and external integrations — the "how".

Rules:
- Web routers in `infrastructure/web/<module>_router.py` — register
  endpoints, call use cases, return responses.
- Persistence adapters in `infrastructure/persistence/<module>_repository.py`
  implement the domain repository interface against a real database
  (SQLAlchemy, Tortoise, or in-memory).
- Infrastructure may import from `domain/`, `application/`, `shared/`,
  and `config/`.

Files per bounded context:
- `web/<module>_router.py` — FastAPI router (endpoints)
- `persistence/<module>_repository.py` — persistence adapter implementing
  the domain interface
